<!--Post: 3563--><!--Time: 1105028654-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3563"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Kayjay<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Kayjay<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 8:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Many similarities to some of the MO&#39;s BTK used: <BR>Killer waited inside the house for victim to return home. <BR>JB was bound tortured and killed in a similar manner to some of BTK&#39;s victims. <BR>JB was found in the basement. <BR>JB wasnt raped but had evidence of sexual assault. <BR>JB&#39;s killer took rope and tape to her home. <BR>JB&#39;s killer liked to &#39;comunicate about himself&#39; as evidenced by a 3 page ransom note. <BR>Boulder isnt all that far from Wichita and its a university town. <BR>JB&#39;s killer signed the note using an acronym S.B.T.C <BR>BTK sent an ID to police in the name of someone from the  <BR>S...outhwestern <BR>B..ell <BR>T..elephone <BR>C..company <BR> <BR>Was BTK to old {frail} by 1996 to take on the whole family? Did he opt just for the young girl? We know from his first killings that the young girl was his main focus. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3563-->
<!--Post: 3568--><!--Time: 1105033392-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3568"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brazilian<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brazilian<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 9:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Look at this: the infamous garrote <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.crimelibrary.com/notorious_murders/famous/ramsey/it_5.html?sect=7" target=_top>http://www.crimelibrary.com/notorious_murders/famo us/ramsey/it_5.html?sect=7</a> <BR> <BR>Personally I dont think this crime has anything to do with BTK, but surely there are some weird coincidences...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3568-->
<!--Post: 4650--><!--Time: 1106620608-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4650"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 24, 2005 - 6:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mrs. Julie Otero seems to be the focus of the first attack, in my opinion. BTK couldn&#39;t have known Josephine was even in the house, as it was a school day. As to JonBenet, not a BTK crime. BTK&#39;s targets were adult women, JonBenet was very high-profile due to the sick performances which pleased her parents, and hundreds of pedophiles witnessed JonBenet; an enormous criminal group were aware of her.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4650-->
<!--Post: 4880--><!--Time: 1106789750-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4880"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Kayjay<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Kayjay<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 5:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I beg to differ George. The young otero girl was found semi naked and hanging in the basement. Its clear which victim was his main focus. <BR>Sick performances? yep, I guess we are on different pages!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4880-->
<!--Post: 5648--><!--Time: 1107234634-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5648"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 9:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The way Josephine was tied is similar to the Barbie doll found on the Ramsey lawn some time after her murder. <BR> <BR>This link is from an archived Ramsey website: <BR><a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20020216224828/http://ramseyfamily.com/barbie.html" target=_top>http://web.archive.org/web/20020216224828/http://r amseyfamily.com/barbie.html</a> <BR> <BR>And the clove hitch knot is similar to the knot used on garrote <BR><a href="http://www.tollesburysc.co.uk/Knots/Clove_hitch1.htm" target=_top>http://www.tollesburysc.co.uk/Knots/Clove_hitch1.h tm</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5648-->
<!--Post: 5697--><!--Time: 1107291298-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5697"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ryddik<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ryddik<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 12:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thats scary the barbie is &#34;bound&#34; the same way. I don&#39;t see someone putting that much effort into strapping fabric to a barbie without having an underlying meaning.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5697-->
<!--Post: 5731--><!--Time: 1107308306-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5731"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 5:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That is scary Ryddik. I think that tying someone at the waist would be unusual.  <BR> <BR>I remembered this from when I would visit the Ramsey Murder message boards. It wasn&#39;t easy to find again.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5731-->
<!--Post: 5755--><!--Time: 1107335147-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5755"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Kayjay<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Kayjay<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 1:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Notice that one of the dolls is wearing a red sock? That addition does appear odd. BTK&#39;s Otero letter makes reference to &#39;sock&#39; in describing both the mother and daughters attire. Has it ever been said what color sock {or socks} Josephine was wearing when found? If the answer is red, then up go the hairs on the back of my neck!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5755-->
<!--Post: 5906--><!--Time: 1107451631-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5906"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 9:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Kayjay, <BR>Another connection to the Ramsey&#39;s could be the city where they had another home,Charlevoix, Michigan. Charlevoix means &#34;Charles voice.&#34; Can&#39;t find that link, but it was on one of Charlevoix&#39;s websites at one time. Charlie is the name of one of the Otero children as we all know.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5906-->
<!--Post: 5910--><!--Time: 1107453458-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5910"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 9:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;Charlevoix means &#34;Charles voice.&#34; <BR>Just another thought. BTK&#39;s voice is on record, the one time he called in Nancy Fox&#39;s murder.  <BR> <BR>Also, Charlie Otero&#39;s initials are CO, which is the abreviation for Colorado. <BR> <BR>The year the Barbie dolls were found on the Ramsey property, 1997, was the 100 anniversary of the Kraft corporation &#40;Post Toasties&#41;. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
