<!--Post: 6352--><!--Time: 1107719498-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6352"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 06, 2005 - 11:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Adding on here: both JonBenet and Josephine&#39;s fathers were pilots.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6352-->
<!--Post: 6361--><!--Time: 1107728568-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6361"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 06, 2005 - 2:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.cbsnews.com/stories/2002/10/01/48hours/main523892.shtml" target=_top>http://www.cbsnews.com/stories/2002/10/01/48hours/ main523892.shtml</a>  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6361-->
<!--Post: 6364--><!--Time: 1107729288-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6364"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 06, 2005 - 2:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Read the part about the cassette tapes and the response the friend got from police and the Tip Line...??? makes you wonder... <BR> <BR>They say his &#40;Oliva&#41; DNA doesn&#39;t match... it took them until 2004 to say the DNA didn&#39;t match the families... <BR> <BR>This is a botched case. <BR> <BR>I feel bad for the parents... the beauty pagent stuff was really inappropriate IMO but to go into a store and see papers calling you a murderer of your own child and a molester and worse... weird or not they don&#39;t and didn&#39;t deserve that. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6364-->
<!--Post: 6541--><!--Time: 1107875769-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6541"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 7:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Q, <BR>I feel bad for the parents too. Many people still believe they did it; I&#39;m not one of those. That case was really botched, but I feel there is still hope. <BR> <BR>One of the serial killers BTK compared himself to was the Boston Strangler. They had that movie on the other night.  <BR> <BR>In the movie it showed a mannequin &#40;undressed like one of the barbie dolls&#41; and there were the words &#34;La Mode&#34; which according to the alta vist translator &#40;French&#41;, means &#34;fashion&#34;. The pageants Jon Benet was in were a lot about fashion, especially some of the one&#39;s she wore. Wasn&#39;t Jon Benet taking French lessons, could be mistaken? <BR> <BR>One of the dolls looks like its taped with a green tape, which is erie in that in BTK&#39;s letter he says she was wearing &#34;green pants.&#34; Maybe the tape is a reflection of the rug.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6541-->
<!--Post: 6555--><!--Time: 1107886573-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6555"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 10:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;One of the dolls looks like its taped with a green tape, which is erie in that in BTK&#39;s letter he says she was wearing &#34;green pants.&#34; Maybe the tape is a reflection of the rug.&#34; -Bookworm <BR> <BR>You lost me there Bookworm... tape...rug??? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6555-->
<!--Post: 6561--><!--Time: 1107889555-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6561"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cyndi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cyndi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 11:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It is also interesting that JonBenet had a RED HEART drawn on the palm of her hand and one of the latest BTK drops was a cereal box with the RED HEART circled.  Coincidence?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
