<!--Post: 6950--><!--Time: 1108089650-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6950"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Kayjay<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Kayjay<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 6:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Several years ago I sent an email to John Ramsey {the family had a web site back then}, outlineing the similarities between his daughters murder and the BTK killings. At the time though, it was a stretch, as there was nothing to indicate that BTK was even alive in 1996. John replied, thanking me etc and saying that he would pass my email on to his investigators. He said that he was convinced that his daughters murder was not the killers first. I was happy knowing that a possible BTK connection was brought to the attention of someone who gave a damn {as opposed to the Boulder LE.} <BR>Something else thats been on my mind for a long time: A couple of years back, a talking head {possibly the guy from AMW...not sure now as it was so long ago} was talking about the Ramsey case on air and his talk included something along the lines of &#34;when John found his daughter hanging in the basement&#34;. The posters in the forum that I frequented at the time, poo poo&#39;ed the idea and said it was just a mistake on his {the talking heads} part. <BR>I suspect it may have been a mistake....the mistake being that he let it slip! He would have been told the details of the killing and if he had not been told of Jonbenet &#39;hanging&#39;, then why on earth would he come out with something like that? <BR>We are told that Jonbenet was found on the floor in the basement which had an overhead pipe. Her wrists had been bound, and there was excess rope extending from those knots. Could it be that she was actually found hanging from the overhead pipe?  Could that explain the excess rope? Some details are kept from the public to weed out loonies who want to confess. Could this detail be one of them? If the talking head had not heard of that detail then I fail to understand why he would mention it, accidently or otherwise!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6950-->
<!--Post: 7037--><!--Time: 1108143281-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7037"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 9:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Josephene was hanged by the neck using a noose. The &#39;head&#39; may had heard about the excess rope and assumed...Or..Ifound a site about a year after the murder that had a lot of info about the initial investigation, including autopsy photos.  <BR>I seem to remember some talk about her being hung up, but i can&#39;t say for sure. The problem stems from the fact that john ramsey &#40;this is wierd&#41; found the body , while the police were in the house already,he either cut her down or picked her body up&#40;the body was in rigor mortis&#41;carried her upstairs and lay the body back on the floor. That was the main thing that cast suspicion his direction. The detectives felt he not only contaminated the crime scene on purpose, but he placed his daughters body on the floor, rather than the kitchen table or a nearby sofa.  <BR> <BR>Of course, I can&#39;t be sure of what is fact, and what is heresay. The jon-bonet case was the most screwed up investigation that I have ever heard of. I actually expected the Boulder police chief and DA to be charged with obstruction for a while there.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7037-->
<!--Post: 7115--><!--Time: 1108188829-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7115"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 10:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->John Ramsey immediately hugged the body of his daughter as soon as she was discovered, thereby contaminating the crime scene.  He also made a very odd statement, claiming her killer didn&#39;t mean to kill her, which is why he put a blanket on her body.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7115-->
<!--Post: 7202--><!--Time: 1108273872-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7202"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 9:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->From BTK letter about Oteros and from section about Josephine regarding the pieces of clothesline used: He said that they were &#34;all one lenght.&#34;  <BR> <BR>When Jon Benet&#39;s autopsy report was released in the press, the word &#34;length&#34; was mispelled similarly, except in the FBI copy of the report. There were other spelling mistakes, and all together they spelled the word &#34;things&#34;. You won&#39;t find copies of these reports anymore, they were obviously corrected. <BR> <BR>BTK said that the pieces of clothesline used on Josephine were &#34;all one lenght.&#34; We don&#39;t know what that length was, but similarly, if you add the lengths of the tails of the ligatures on each of Jon Benet&#39;s wrist and garotte, they are equal. So I would assume her murderer measured these lengths so they were the same. 15.5&#43;5.5=21  17&#43;4=21 <BR> <BR>From the autopsy report: <BR>Right wrist. <BR>“At the knot there is one tail end which measures 5.5 inches in length with a frayed end. The other tail of the knot measures 15.5 inches in length and ends in a double loop knot.  <BR>This end of the cord is also frayed.” <BR> <BR>Garotte <BR>“Extending from the knot…are two tails of the knot, one measuring 4 inches in length and having a frayed end, and the other measuring 17 inches in length  with the end tied in multiple loops around a length of a round tan-brown wooden stick which measures 4.5 inches in length.” <BR> <BR>Another similarity is that the Ramsey ransom note was found on the bottom stairs and BTK says that&#39;s where some of Josephine&#39;s clothes were &#40;basement stairs&#41;. <BR> <BR>BTK also mentions a &#34;dryer or freezer&#34; in the basement. I can&#39;t be absolutely positive, but I thought that Jon Benet&#39;s blanket had been in the dryer and that&#39;s where they thought it was taken from. I have to review the books. <BR> <BR>Ed the description of how the blanket was on Jon Benet was different in Douglas&#39;s book and Schiller&#39;s book. I don&#39;t understand why French didn&#39;t look in that room when he first searched the house.  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7202-->
<!--Post: 7313--><!--Time: 1108397206-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7313"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 8:06 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;all one lenght.&#34; <BR>Rereading this, BTK could have meant he used one piece of clothes line, rather than several like I thought. <BR> <BR>&#34;things&#34; <BR>The Boston Strangler used the word &#34;thing&#34; to describe the &#34;cord&#34; from the blue bathrobe of his first victim Anna Slesers in 1962.&#40;J.Brussel, M.D.&#41; <BR> <BR>The Boston Strangler had other names for crimes he was arrested for. The first was the &#34;Measuring Man,&#34; because posing as a model scout, he was measuring young women from their bust to their ankles. Served time for this. <BR> <BR>The other name the BS was given was the &#34;Green Man&#34; for his &#34;green coveralls, green glasses, and sometimes green gloves.&#34; He had quit killing and had become &#34;an insatiable sex-seeker&#34; at the time he was caught.&#40;Brussel&#41; <BR> <BR>I thought this name was interesting because of &#34;green cards.&#34;  Hispanic workers have to have them if they are working in the US. The Oteros were hispanic and so was the Ramsey housekeeper, not that they needed green cards. <BR> <BR>The BS was good at talking his way into women&#39;s homes, even at the height of his murder rampage.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7313-->
<!--Post: 10137--><!--Time: 1109782016-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10137"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Beckyks<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Beckyks<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 8:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The barbie doll thing seems really weird/coincidental now that they&#39;ve told us that BTK left a pj doll in his package.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
