<!--Post: 10270--><!--Time: 1109867604-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10270"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jilleng<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jilleng<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 8:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here are 2 links for JBR...the first is the ransom note...the 2nd is the autopsy...the  wording in JBR&#39;s autopsy in my opinion very similar to BTK victim autopsys... <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.thesmokinggun.com/archive/ransom1.html" target=_top>http://www.thesmokinggun.com/archive/ransom1.html</a> <BR><a href="http://www.thesmokinggun.com/archive/jonbenet2.html" target=_top>http://www.thesmokinggun.com/archive/jonbenet2.htm l</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10270-->
<!--Post: 10575--><!--Time: 1110029644-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10575"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 05, 2005 - 5:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Jonbenet&#39;s Barbie PJ&#39;s were found with her weren&#39;t they? <BR> <BR>Kayjay, <BR>I&#39;m glad you brought Jonbenet&#39;s case up. I bet Jonbenet&#39;s detectives didn&#39;t connect the Barbie dolls found with the BTK case or they may have found with the WPD&#39;s help that the dolls were bound similar to Josephine.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
