<!--Post: 11709--><!--Time: 1111037597-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11709"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 16, 2005 - 9:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->E - Mr. Smits&#39; office is not far from mine, and you know where I am. We didn&#39;t live here very long when this happened to JonBenet. My daughter is the same age. I was, I guess thrown back into defense mode after leaving Wichita. I couldn&#39;t begin to imagine who would do this to such a beautiful child. I in my heart I never believed that JonBenet&#39;s parents had anything to do with this crime. Just like in my heart I always knew that BTK had murdered Marine. My heart broke for Patsy, John, and Burke Ramsey. JonBenet was going to be the next Ms. Colorado and for all we knew the next Ms. America. She was beautiful, I was very proud of her and she wasn&#39;t even my child. JonBenet was a mirror of the Colorado Rockies and we would have been well represented. All I good invision was that she would blow Ms. Texas off the map. Yeah! Anyway, the Boulder PD was pathetic. When I found out when they released her DNA for testing I almost fell over. The Boulder PD was like a soap opera. Instead of really putting forth a good faith effort into finding out who did that to this beautiful child, they got lazy and humdum and focused everything on Patsy and John. I have to admit, the ransom note was a bit puzzeling. It did request the exact amount of Mr. Ramsey&#39;s bonus. How many people would know what his bonus was going to be?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
