<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12239"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 25, 2005 - 2:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I could be very wrong but it seems that BTK always was able to move throughout neighborhoods &amp; the community due to his uniform/public service position.  <BR> <BR>Hiding in plain site. <BR> <BR>Was the Ramsey home completely isolated so that BTK could drive a car to the home undetected and not be seen by potential witnesses ?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
