<!--Post: 12441--><!--Time: 1112230674-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12441"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 30, 2005 - 4:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A few more coincidences? Perhaps Rader was at his father&#39;s bedside on December 26, 1996? <BR> <BR>Under the &#34;Facts About Dennis Rader&#34; thread it is said the his father died on December 27, 1996, which happens to be the day after Jon Benet was killed, the day she was actually found. <BR> <BR>In the ransom note, P.2, the Ramsey&#39;s are warned &#34;If we catch you talking to a stray dog, she dies.&#34;  Very odd for any ransom note. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
