<!--Post: 12973--><!--Time: 1113892167-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12973"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 18, 2005 - 11:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky..I am sorry about Marine..I have read about all the victims and she seems like a nice lady..My heart goes out to you, your mom, the families of the victims, and their friends... <BR>and yes I agree BTK is a monster....but how could you tie him to John Benet ?..Had he ever seen Jon Benet ? Did he know her family ?How often had he been to Boulder? And there&#39;s still that ransom note...and I am perplexed by that as well as it seems to imply the killer knew about the money John Ramsey was expecting to receive...How would the killer know that ?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12973-->
<!--Post: 12983--><!--Time: 1113918253-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12983"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 19, 2005 - 6:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky, <BR>What is DTDC? <BR> <BR>Angry, <BR>118,000 ransom: notice that the date of Beth&#39;s death is in 118, with &#34;no one&#34; 1/08. <BR> <BR>Here are more coincidences. <BR>Beth Ramsey was&#40;k&#41;illed with her boyfriend in Chicago in a collision with a &#40;b&#41;akery &#40;t&#41;ruck. &#34;btk&#34;. I read this in one of the books on JonBenet but can&#39;t remember which one. It wasn&#39;t DOI or PMPT. <BR> <BR>In the book Cady&#39;s son was killed by a delivery truck and said he would like to return the favor in kind to other of his victims. <BR> <BR>Cady was released from an Indiana prison. Santa&#39;s daughter, age 9, and a friend were kidnapped, the friend molested, in Indiana. The perp wasn&#39;t caught. This was December 26, 1974. The first year of BTK. &#40;DOI,HB,p.167&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12983-->
<!--Post: 12984--><!--Time: 1113919018-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12984"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 19, 2005 - 6:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Book - DTDC is: Denny the dog catcher! &#40;I think, it was LostDog that coined that phrase back in February&#41;HA! BTW-your awesome at picking up those details and or coincidences. You go honey! <BR> <BR>Angry - those are all legitimate questions. I&#39;ve been trying to start with one in general, was DTDC in Boulder Colorado December of 1996? If I recall correctly, the Ramsey&#39;s had an ADT Security system on their house. The question about the ransom note I mentioned in a previous post. Then again, on a different note, how did DTDC get from 21st &amp; Woodlawn &#40;where he dropped off Marine&#39;s car&#41;back to his home. Did he have help?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
