<!--Post: 13070--><!--Time: 1114066690-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13070"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 20, 2005 - 11:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->What was denny&#39;s job when Marine was killed ? <BR>If he worked for Park City..he had a police type radio..he could have called someone..or maybe there was a park City employee in the area..denny calls him up, makes up a story, and gets a ride back to his house... <BR>But if someone  unknowingly gave him a lift...have they come forward and will there be any testimony from them at the trial...   ? <BR>Thank you Rocky for helping me out at the other thread... <BR>I write a little thread at <a href="http://WWW.WATE.COM" target=_top>WWW.WATE.COM</a> about crime..if you ever get bored come over and read it or post something..Take care...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13070-->
<!--Post: 13100--><!--Time: 1114181405-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13100"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 22, 2005 - 7:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There was a great documentary on Court TV last night about JonBenet.  WHole new set of detectives...they have found DNA evidence that the BOulder police completely ignored...now they can&#39;t get them to reinvestigate because it has been so long. <BR>ALso, the Ramseys are now impoverished. <BR>I guess Patsy had ovarian cancer and when it came back she did not have any health insurance and Mr. Ramsey cannot find work. <BR>It is a great show and they have positive suspects and leads and now positive evidence but with the lack of cooperation of Boulder...the murderer still walks the streets. <BR>I do believe this show is being repeated so check your guide... <BR>very informative <BR>very upseting <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13100-->
<!--Post: 13101--><!--Time: 1114181473-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13101"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 22, 2005 - 7:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Watch this... <BR>it WILL shock you <BR>Shame on the law enforcement of Boulder <BR>If I was the Ramsey&#39;s I would seriously sue them<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13101-->
<!--Post: 13127--><!--Time: 1114221023-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13127"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 22, 2005 - 6:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Angry- Denny worked for ADT when Marine was murdered in 1985. &#40;I lived across the street from him at the time.&#41;He became the Park City compliance officer in 1991. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m really sorry that you have had more than your fair share of life&#39;s cruel surprises. You know there are other&#39;s here that have had similar experiences, maybe you all should get together and share that with each other. You know my Mom always told me &#34;God isn&#39;t suppose to put any more on you than you can handle.&#34; Somedays I wonder about that too! God Bless! <BR> <BR>Else - I caught bits and pieces of it last night. I knew that they didn&#39;t send JB&#39;s DNA off until last year to be tested and compared to the perp. I&#39;m tellin you the Boulder PD should be investigated by the US Attorney General&#39;s office. That&#39;s pathetic.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13127-->
<!--Post: 13132--><!--Time: 1114264851-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13132"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 23, 2005 - 7:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Else and Rocky, <BR>I saw the show too. They didn&#39;t give you anyone to contact if you have any info though. Did you see all those boxes of tips, etc.? They believe the killer&#39;s name may be in one. <BR> <BR>I found my reference for the bakery truck. It was in Steve Thomas&#39;s book &#40;HB p.135&#41; <BR> <BR>Moved to Boulder the middle of 1991. John Ramsey in a deposition.  1991 has the date of  Dee Davis’s murder 1/19. Beth died 1/08/92  If you subtract the difference of the two dates, length of time, it’s 354 days. 3/45 is coincidentally, the month and year of Radar’s birthdate. The day before Dee’s death is 1/18 a number in the ransom note. <BR><a href="http://web.dailycamera.com/extra/ramsey/2000/0206deposition.html" target=_top>http://web.dailycamera.com/extra/ramsey/2000/0206d eposition.html</a> <BR> <BR>Delores &#40;Dee&#41; Davis 1/19/1991 <BR><a href="http://www.mercurynews.com/mld/mercurynews/11002825.htm?template=contentModules/printstory.jsp" target=_top>http://www.mercurynews.com/mld/mercurynews/1100282 5.htm?template=contentModules/printstory.jsp</a> <BR> <BR>One more similarity. John Ramsey was affiliated with the company Sun Microsystems &#40;in deposition link&#41;, BB worked for Sunrooms &#40;NIW&#41;, and the symbol for the Coleman company is a sun. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13132-->
<!--Post: 13138--><!--Time: 1114285946-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13138"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 23, 2005 - 12:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Marine Hedge <BR>Marine is similar to Marino. In some of the books, Jim Marino was named as a suspect by the Ramsey’s &#40;PMPT, PB, P.579&#41; In Cyril Wecht and Charles Bosworth, Jr’s book, Who Killed JonBenet?, PB, P. 135-137, it shows Marino had been a friend of John Ramsey’s since about 1977. Marino had teased Ramsey about Patsy being John’s Jackie Kennedy. &#40;Lee Harvey Oswald&#39;s wife&#39;s name is Marina.&#41; <BR> <BR>Also, in 1986 &#40;the murders of Dee and Marine-1985&#41;, John had hired a secretary. She was fingerprinted, just to check, as with others, with the one on the ransom note. &#40;PMPT, p. 138-140&#41;. She was cleared. I know this is way out in left field but I’m just trying to compare what was happening with the Ramseys at this time. LW had worked for Ramsey for 10 years and at the time of JonBenet’s death. <BR> <BR>Also, according to the Marine Hedge threads on this board, pine tree needles were found on her. According to the maid, &#40;PMPT&#41;JonBenet was found in the room the Ramsey’s kept their Christmas trees. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13138-->
<!--Post: 13140--><!--Time: 1114303071-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13140"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 23, 2005 - 5:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Book - your research skills are awesome! There are some amazing coincidences here. Your attention to details are too! What do you do for a living? BTW -it is suspected that Marine Hedge had pine needles on her because her and Tom had at the time two big pine trees in their front yard. I&#39;m sure they were in her car and stayed with her person.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13140-->
<!--Post: 13152--><!--Time: 1114318230-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13152"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 23, 2005 - 9:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Rocky, <BR>I just use a lot of my spare time on this, and have a lot of the books handy. I like the one&#39;s with indexes. I&#39;m still reading Nightmare in Wichita. <BR> <BR>There are plenty of coincidences. Another is that a lady by the last name of Dillon lived behind the Ramsey&#39;s.&#40;PMPT&#41; <BR> <BR>I got this from the Marine Hedge thread by Verm_inve post. He posted that Marine had an evergreen tree on her. But there were needles in her car. <BR>&#34;covered with tall grass and an evergreen tree in a ditch&#34; <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13152-->
<!--Post: 13175--><!--Time: 1114456871-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13175"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 25, 2005 - 12:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->EVERYTHING about the JB case is pathetic and ridiculous.  The Boulder PD completely dropped the ball on everything. EVERTHING.  Now it is probably to late to track down the killer&#40;s&#41;.  Boulder makes the WPD look like saints.  The Ramsy&#39;s lives are completely and !00% ruined...especially at the hands of the BOULDER PD and DA<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13175-->
<!--Post: 13176--><!--Time: 1114460046-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13176"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 25, 2005 - 1:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Elsewhere, <BR>Personally, I think there is still hope in solving JonBenet&#39;s murder.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13176-->
<!--Post: 13193--><!--Time: 1114525892-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13193"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 26, 2005 - 7:31 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Book - oh I agree. I don&#39;t think the group of PI&#39;s are gonna give up now....especially when they can shove it up Boulder&#39;s PD a&#42;&#42;&#39;s.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13193-->
<!--Post: 13204--><!--Time: 1114532360-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13204"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 26, 2005 - 9:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Book - the evergreen tree would be completely out of place. In that neck of the woods there are elm, cottowood etc., but nothing like an evergreen tree. Which inturn makes me wonder about that. Tall grass is certainly possible. <BR> <BR>I as well think that there is still hope in solving JonBenet&#39;s murder. The show we all watched was certainly encouraging.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13204-->
<!--Post: 13205--><!--Time: 1114533034-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13205"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 26, 2005 - 9:30 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky - was thee by chance an evergreen tree in Marine&#39;s yard...or close by. <BR>Do you remember? <BR> <BR>Also, won&#39;t it be interesting to watch the JB case unfold...hope there will be more info on it. <BR>I&#39;m gonna check the site AMW...maybe there. <BR>Have a great day<IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13205-->
<!--Post: 13231--><!--Time: 1114610963-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13231"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Kayjay<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Kayjay<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 27, 2005 - 7:09 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It sure would be interesting to know what brand of security alarm the Ramsey&#39;s had in their house {if any posters live near there, just go knock on the door and ask the present owners!} <BR>Security companies would have house plans showing the details of where each device was located, sensors, motion detectors, switches etc {at least one would think}. If the installer where prone to sneak into houses uninvited, then a copy of the layout of the house interior could come in handy one day.... <BR>The BPD always said that the killer had to be someone familiar with the house interior, since it was so complex, however I dont believe anything the BPD said since its ultimately been proven that they didnt know sh&#42;t from clay in that investigation. <BR>Just a thought.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
