<!--Post: 13524--><!--Time: 1115484869-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13524"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, May 07, 2005 - 9:54 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I finished reading NIW. In the book it said that an SBT Business card was found in one of the BTK packages/letter, May, 2004.  <BR> <BR>Business was spelled as bussiness in the Ramsey ransom note, signed SBTC.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
