<!--Post: 14168--><!--Time: 1125073472-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST14168"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, August 26, 2005 - 9:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Found this article, very good. Near the last part, this reporter talks to some of &#34;140&#34; suspects.  <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.boulderweekly.com/archive/122001/coverstory.html" target=_top>http://www.boulderweekly.com/archive/122001/covers tory.html</a> <BR> <BR>Another thought, dogface uses SBT for sparky big time. <BR> <BR>sparky being an erection<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 14168-->
<!--Post: 14207--><!--Time: 1125440312-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST14207"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, August 30, 2005 - 3:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Jonbenet&#39;s pageant schedule: <BR> <BR>January 1995 - PAGEANTS <BR>. <BR>JonBenét participated in the Charlevoix pageant in July of 1994 and enjoyed it - - so Patsy looked for others.There was a little contest at the Twin Peaks Mall, not far from Boulder. According to Larry Schiller, Patsy entered JonBenét but she was ignored by the judges. <BR>. <BR>In June, 1995, JonBenét was crowned Little Miss Charlevoix - spent the rest of the summer riding in convertibles in various home-town parades throughout Michigan. <BR> <BR>September 1995 - JonBenét participated in Miss Sunburst Pageant at the Twin Peaks Mall in Longmont, Colorado. <BR> <BR>In October, JonBenét become Little Miss Colorado <BR> <BR> <BR>Between 1995 and 1996, JonBenét would be Colorado State All Star Kids Cover Girl, National Tiny Miss Beauty, America&#39;s Royale Miss, Colorado Dream Girl, Miss Sunburst Colorado and Little Miss Merry Christmas. <BR> <BR>So that&#39;s one in 1994, 3 in 1995. More in 1996, but less than 6. The last three I have notes on were as follows:  <BR> <BR>. <BR>Right after Thanksgiving, 1996 - that weekend JonBenét was part of a pageant in Rome, Ga. her mother would buy a white dress from another participant - that dress would be the one JonBenét would be buried in. <BR>. <BR>December 17th, 1996 - JonBenét entered the All Star Kids Christmas Pageant at the Airport Holiday Inn just outside Denver. She won several titles, Including Little Miss Merry Christmas. <BR>. <BR>JonBenét was expected to be a participant in the Little Miss Hawaiian Tropic Pageant on January 5th, 1997. She didn&#39;t live to see the day.....  <BR> <BR>END <BR> <BR>Hmmm, Rader had a project he called <BR>&#34;project twin peaks&#34; <BR> <BR>in one letter after arrest he said he was working on a golden star, jonbenet wore an outfit in one of the pageants that looked like a golden star. <BR> <BR>in one letter he said <BR>&#34;when in rome&#34; <BR>jonbenet was in a pageant in Rome Georgia. <BR> <BR>Miss USA was held in wichita in 93, maybe dogface got hooked on beauty queens at that time. <BR> <BR>Tavia &#40;Shackles&#41; Hunt represented the state of Kansas at the 1993 Miss USA pageant in Wichita, Kansas.  <BR> <BR>Here is a link to an article about the boulder police recieveing an annonomous letter in 97 from shrevesport where the the 97 miss usa pageant was held, the letter is about Jonbonet, and also in the article it tells how there is 2 weeks of activities prior to the pageant, and that hundreds of little girls were all over the place for the 2 weeks. Not saying that Jonbenet was there in wichita, but lots of other little beauty queens were. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.google.com/search?q=cache:Xk9KgSl_b40J:63.147.65.175/news/jon7.htm%2B%2B%22miss%2Busa%2Bpageant%22%2Bjonbenet&amp;hl=en&amp;lr=lang_en" target=_top>http://www.google.com/search?q=cache:Xk9KgSl_b40J: 63.147.65.175/news/jon7.htm&#43;&#43;%22miss&#43;usa&#43;pageant%2 2&#43;jonbenet&amp;hl=en&amp;lr=lang_en</a> <BR> <BR> <BR>Coincidence?  To me, it is not. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 14207-->
<!--Post: 14208--><!--Time: 1125440430-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST14208"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, August 30, 2005 - 3:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Oh, I forgoet to mention something I learned recently, near jonbenet&#39;s body in the basement was an unopened christmas gift. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
