<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST14255"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, September 02, 2005 - 8:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bookworm...no not the Enquirer...I read it in the 92 pages document of the investigation..the arrest and the interrogation and statments of 83707.  The celebrity binder was just one of many of his binder scrapbooks.  I was sure I printed that document from kansas.com - it was very informative as I could only watch the sentencing via the internet so there were portions I didn&#39;t get to hear and also they did not cover every bit of evidence they found.  Anyways...now I can&#39;t find that on Kansas.com anymore and I threw my copy away after reading it...I was so taken back.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
